Privacy Policy

Effective August 26, 2026

PixelGraph is designed to keep your creative work on your device. This policy explains the limited information used to provide subscriptions and operate the app.

Creative content

Projects, imported textures, custom nodes, and export settings are stored locally on your device. PixelGraph does not upload your project content to a PixelGraph account or server. Content only leaves your device when you choose to export or share it using iPadOS.

Subscriptions and diagnostics

PixelGraph uses RevenueCat to manage subscriptions. RevenueCat may process an anonymous app user identifier, purchase and entitlement status, app version, device and operating-system information, and subscription-related diagnostics. Apple processes App Store purchases and payment information under Apple’s own privacy terms. PixelGraph does not receive your full payment-card details.

This information is used only to show available plans, complete or restore purchases, verify access to PixelGraph Pro, diagnose subscription failures, and prevent fraud.

Sharing, sale, and advertising

PixelGraph does not sell your personal information and does not use third-party advertising trackers. Subscription information is shared only with service providers needed to operate App Store purchases and entitlement verification.

Retention and your choices

Project data remains on your device until you delete it or remove the app. Subscription records are retained by Apple and RevenueCat according to their legal and operational requirements. You can manage or cancel subscriptions in your Apple ID settings and can restore purchases from the PixelGraph paywall.

Children and changes

PixelGraph is a creative tool and is not directed to children under 13. This policy may be updated when the app’s data practices or service providers change. The effective date above identifies the current version.

Contact

For privacy questions or requests, use the developer support contact listed on PixelGraph’s App Store product page.
